this last september i chose to ditch  apple's large max model phones and for  the first time since i can remember go  with the smaller 6.1 inch model and now  that it has been four months was it  worth trading in that large gorgeous 6.7  inch screen and the much larger battery  for a more reasonable phone or did i  make a mistake and wish that i got the  max model like i did last year and the  previous years before that in this video  i will go over what my concerns were  finally making the jump and ditching the  max if those came to light and if the  iphone 13 pro is worth buying or if you  should just get the max let's start out  with why i wanted a smaller phone in the  first place but never bought one and how  the phone world has changed so much in  just over a decade when apple announced  their iphone the three and a half inch  display was considered a large screen  bigger than my first smartphone the  google htc g1 but shortly after that  android manufacturers started making  screens larger and larger my second  phone was the original samsung galaxy s  and what sold me on it was the huge  gorgeous display at a massive 4 inches  which sounds hilarious now with screen  sizes that we have but when i saw the  galaxy note i knew i had to have it even  though i was making barely any money at  the time i saved up and i bought one  because i love the idea of the s-pen and  that huge 5.3 inch display which  actually sounds small now that phone  proved that people wanted phablets and  it really propelled the whole android  market since apple wanted to stick to  small screens for many years three years  later they finally caved and had to  start making large screen phones and  that is what finally got me to buy into  apple's ecosystem with the iphone 6 plus  and i became a big apple fan now like  most tech enthusiasts i stayed with  their large screen phones because they  offered much better battery life than  the smaller phones along with exclusive  features the biggest one probably being  portrait mode which was a game changer  and it started the demise of dedicated  cameras for most people as the years  went on the big iphones kept growing and  growing both in size and weight with the  iphone 13 pro max being 240 grams now  close to 50 percent heavier than the  original big iphone and weighing closer  now to the z full 3 which is a much  bigger phone so as these phones got  bigger and heavier at some point it just  got unwieldy but i still stuck with the  larger ones because of the regular  iphones they're just too small the 4.7  inch ones um and even the 5.8 up until  the iphone 10r came out with a 6.1 inch  screen which i absolutely love that size  of it was like the old goldilocks story  the 10r fit perfectly in my hand where  the 10s was too small and the 10s max  was a bit too large but of course apple  still gave enough reasons for me to keep  buying the big phones even up until the  iphone 12 series because if you cared  about having the best camera quality and  i do you have to buy the 12 pro max for  its superior cameras but this year for  the first time ever apple made a change  that we weren't expecting with the  iphone 13 lineup they finally stopped  forcing people to buy the biggest phone  if they wanted the best or the full set  of features the smaller iphone 13 pro  has the same exact camera system with  the same updated ultra wide the three  times telephoto and the larger main  sensor now they did put in one  limitation if you buy the base 128 gig  model you can't shoot prores video in 4k  but only 1080p in an attempt i think to  get more people to spend extra money to  get the larger capacity and of course  that's exactly what i ended up doing for  the first time ever i purchased myself  the smaller iphone and because the 13  pro cost a hundred dollars less even  with that extra storage i still ended up  paying the same i would have for a base  level 13 pro max so how has it been did  my concerns come true and has the  battery life been good enough compared  to having that massive battery of the  max well first off i want to comment on  that prores and if spending the extra  for the larger storage was worth it now  i've always bought the base storage  amount with iphones for two reasons the  first being resale now i'm obviously  somebody who upgrades phones every year  i kind of need to do that for my job and  i sell my older ones and if you're  somebody that's looked online at use  prices with the iphones that have more  storage they don't really sell for much  more than just the base amount and with  that apple charges way too much money to  upgrade storage in my opinion and second  i've been using icloud for many years  now so i don't really need the extra  space with that said within the last  year or so i started noticing that my  phone kept having a buffer because my  photo library has grown so much that  everything has started to stream and the  local photos are really low quality and  a lot of the videos they wouldn't even  play if i don't have internet connection  because they're all stored completely up  in the cloud and that started to get  really annoying at times the whole 1080p  prores really pushed me over that edge  and finally got me to spend extra on  more storage because how could i a video  shooter be forced to shoot 1080p video  in 2021 right well four months later i  am not shooting prores at all for me it  was not enough of a quality difference  to be you know willing to spend extra  time the extra capacity to actually use  it so if you're somebody that is  wondering about that and thinking about  spending extra money on storage for that  i wouldn't do it i will say though that  i don't remember the last time that i  had to buffer video or wait for a photo  to display in better quality which has  been really nice so i'm glad that i  finally got the 256 days of storage and  thanks to downsizing to a smaller phone  it didn't cost me any extra compared to  previous years now by far my biggest  concern going with the smaller iphone  this year was the battery life larger  iphones have always had much bigger  batteries inside and even though the 13  lineup has grown as far as battery life  overall the max model grew the most now  over 40 percent larger battery compared  to the 13 pro so i wondered if i would  struggle with battery life going with  the smaller phone so how has the battery  life been over the last four months well  to be honest at first it was a bit of a  pain 13 pro max was getting absolutely  insane battery life but i wasn't getting  through a full day with my 13 pro like i  had with my previous 12 pro max and at  one point i was so close to upgrading to  a max and selling my regular pro just  because i was getting annoyed with  constantly having the battery died  before the day was over unless i plugged  in some time during the day thankfully  battery life actually got quite a bit  better after about a month or so and i  can now get through a full day and still  have about 10 to 15 battery left when i  go to plug it in and charge it at night  with my mac safe charger even though i'm  still using it the same so i'm really  glad that i did not ditch it and go back  to the max now that is pretty much  exactly what i got with my 12 pro max  and better than what i had with my 11  pro max so it definitely isn't a  downside now my only guess is that this  is because of software optimization and  when the 13s came out with ios 15  software just wasn't well optimized  enough for the a15 processor and the new  features that it packed but now that it  has been the battery life is fantastic  now sure the 13 pro max can get some  people through two full days of use but  for most people that charge their phone  every night anyways the deciding point  is really if that phone can get through  a full day without needing to be plugged  in or charged and for the first time  ever a regular sized iphone can do that  even for power users like myself which  is really impressive because i have a  ton of apps on here that are always  running in the background and looking at  location and things like that so if  you're somebody that's been wanting to  go to a smaller phone and you are  hesitant don't be and give it a try i  think you'll be pleasantly surprised now  how has it been sacrificing the huge  gorgeous screen and how has the comfort  been going with the smaller phone well i  have to say that i love this smaller  phone the 6.1 inch size is perfect in  the hand as i can actually use it  one-handed without any issues and that  has been really nice now when i go back  and pick up a pro max it feels unwieldy  and i remember having to deal with that  all the time in order to get the  top-of-the-line features and the all-day  battery now as far as media do i miss  having that huge screen well for videos  no not at all you actually just get used  to the slightly smaller screen and then  you don't even notice it and for  websites and doing things like that  everything is just a little bit smaller  so you still get the same amount of  usable screen real estate i will say  that for gaming that is the one area  where i do sometimes wish that i had the  larger display especially with shooting  games like call of duty where you have a  lot going on a lot of things on the  screen but of course it's still  perfectly playable now overall i will  say that after finally deciding to ditch  the massive max size phone or the plus  models in the past and finally going  with this model or one i'm really happy  that i did and i have no regrets and i  really hope that the iphone 14 line up  that one also doesn't have any  limitations with the smaller one and  they don't add any extra features to the  max model and if that's the case then i  will still go with the 6.1 inch size so  overall after finally ditching the  massive max phone and going with a  smaller model i'm really happy that i  did that and i have no regrets of course  the phone is a huge improvement compared  to the iphone 12 lineup especially with  the battery life and the cameras but  also with 5g speeds and most of all the  graphics performance without having any  screen dimming or very little compared  to the iphone 12. i really hope that  apple keeps the iphone 14s the same and  they don't give the max model exclusive  features over the regular pro so i can  stick with the smaller size so if you're  somebody that wants to buy an iphone 13  and you're not sure if you just go for  the pro model or spend extra for the max  i would say if you've been wanting to go  for a smaller phone that's more  comfortable now is the time and i think  you'll be very happy thank you guys for  watching check out our long term review  on the iphone 13 pro max over there or  one of our comparisons click above to  subscribe if you guys want to help us  reach our goal of 1 million subscribers  this is max and i'll see you in the next  video  [Music]

